# AGENTS.md

[[.Name]] is a Weft app: Go serves the API and the pages the build writes, in one binary. Weft [[.Version]] is unpacked in `.weft/`, which `weft` writes and you do not edit.

## Commands

```sh
weft dev        # run the app, rebuilding pages and Go as you save
weft build      # build the pages, then the binary
weft upgrade    # move the app to the Weft version of the weft you run
go test -tags dev ./...   # the Go tests
pnpm typecheck  # check the Vue files
```

Go commands need `-tags dev` until the first `weft build`: without it `dist.go` embeds `web/dist`, which does not exist yet.

## Layout

| Path | What it is |
| --- | --- |
| `main.go`, `dist.go`, `dist_dev.go` | The server. `dist.go` embeds `web/dist` and listens on every interface; with `-tags dev`, as `weft dev` builds it, `dist_dev.go` embeds nothing and listens on 127.0.0.1 only |
| `api/` | The Go API, under `/api` |
| `web/pages/` | One page per `.vue` file; its path is the route |
| `web/components/` | Your components; an island is one used with `Island` |

## Rules

- Every component is `<script setup vapor lang="ts">`. Never use the Options API, `getCurrentInstance` or VNode render functions.
- Weft components (`Page`, `Card`, `Button` and the rest) need no import in a `.vue` file. `useHead` is a function, so import it from `@weft/ui`.
- Styles use only `--weft-*` tokens, each with a fallback.
- Components adapt from inside; do not write a mobile variant of a component.
- The components, their props and examples are in `.weft/catalog/components.json`.
- The Go code uses the standard library and `github.com/flakerimi/weft`.
- More for agents: https://weft.base.al/llms.txt
